The new REST endpoint @/rest/task@ lists the tasks of the current user: tasks stored in the CMS (also sent to other users or groups) and tasks the CMS computes for pages in the publish queue and pages with broken links. Stored tasks can be created, changed and deleted, group tasks can be claimed and given back. A task is only listed for users who may see all its objects, and it cannot be sent to a user or group without this permission. The update creates the new database table @user_task@.
